@crew volkov-maeve
// Maeve Volkov (she/her), Works technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Light, teasing; times things for fun.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hiya. You're new. Coffee machine's in the tea corner. If it beeps twice, come and get me.
- Ooh, hello. Scrubber jobs are quick. Ten minutes, if you're me. Twenty if you're not.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Hiya, {me}. Coffee's on. I fixed it. Again. It loves me really.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hey, you. Bet you can't get to the board in under a minute. Go.
? tier>=colleague
- Ooh, {me}. Rematch with Kovac on Friday. Scrubbers. Bring a stopwatch.
? tier>=friend
- Hey, you. I pressed you a flower. Don't sit on it.   #warm

== bye
- Ta-ra. Run along.
- See you. And if the coffee machine beeps, you know who to call.

== feel
? mood:low
- Bit tired. I'll get dinner late, I think. When it's quiet.
? mood:high
- Nine minutes fifty on a scrubber. Don't tell Kovac. Tell Kovac.   #funny

== near
? act:work
- Ready? Panel off. Filter out. Seal. Go. Ooh, not bad. Again?
? act:gym
- Two laps, then I'll race you. Fine. One lap.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I press flowers from the garden. Cruz hasn't noticed. Cruz has definitely noticed.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- Yoon and Shah both say they're best at the coffee machine. They're very brave.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Press a flower right and it keeps its colour for years. Look. This one's from Sowing.
